# State messages are declared ahead of the modules that render them (M2–M11).
state.* — Global/session notices are reserved for screens and flows implemented in later milestones.
auth.* — Authentication and account-security screens are implemented by later identity tasks.
setup.* — Setup wizard messages are implemented by later admin/setup tasks.
today.* — Today screen messages are implemented by the execution milestone.
progress.* — Progress screens are implemented by the execution milestone.
session.* — Focus-session messages are implemented by the execution milestone.
task.* — Task surfaces and state transitions are implemented by the planning and execution milestones.
tasks.* — Task-list empty states are implemented by the planning milestone.
goal.* — Goal surfaces are implemented by the planning milestone.
goals.* — Goal-list empty states are implemented by the planning milestone.
workspace.* — Workspace surfaces are implemented by the planning milestone.
conflict.* — Conflict states are consumed by later module screens.
stale.* — Stale-data states are consumed by later module screens.
schedule.* — Schedule states are implemented by the scheduler milestone.
placement.* — Placement explanations are implemented by the scheduler milestone.
unplaced.* — Scheduler explanation states are implemented by the scheduler milestone.
landscape.* — Fixed-commitment and calendar-import screens are implemented by the landscape milestone.
sync.* — Offline sync surfaces are implemented by the sync milestone.
notes.* — Note surfaces are implemented by the knowledge milestone.
note.* — Note save states are implemented by the knowledge milestone.
search.* — Note search is implemented by the knowledge milestone.
canvas.* — Canvas surfaces are implemented by the canvas milestone.
ai.* — AI states are implemented by the AI milestone.
data.* — Data export and deletion screens are implemented by the admin milestone.
admin.* — Admin screens are implemented by the admin milestone.
billing.* — Billing screens are implemented by the billing milestone.
term.* — Terminology keys are reserved for template-aware surfaces.
error.* — Error-code messages are consumed by the error mapper task T-048.
email.* — Email messages are consumed by server-side email templates, not web/src.
nav.* — shell and settings labels
settings.* — shell and settings labels
module.canvas.name — T-050 disabled Canvas route placeholder
